# NorthernKnife — UGC Scripting

This repo powers UGC script production: take a persona + product + moment +
offer, and produce creator-ready **talking-head scripts** with iPhone-only
shoot direction and a shared b-roll list.

Brand: NorthernKnife (https://northernknife.com/) — hand-forged,
Viking-inspired knives.

Sibling repo: `my-client` (daily TrendTrack → Notion video-brief routine).
Same brand, same copy rulebook, **different deliverable** — that repo writes
ad briefs for an editor, this one writes words a real person says to a phone
camera. Don't cross-paste output between the two.

## Read this first

`brand-pack/START-HERE.md` is the entry point to the creative reference
library (brand voice, personas, creator direction, approved scripts, and the
exact UGC deliverable spec). Read it before writing any script.

**The single most important file is
`brand-pack/05-process/ugc-script-process.md`.** Section D defines the *exact*
script deliverable block by block. Section C is the copy-voice rulebook
(banned spec-sheet jargon, hook patterns, offer rules). Section E is the
creative-direction + b-roll spec. Section F is the pre-flight gate — run it
on every script before delivery.

The house UGC format in this workspace is the `chopper` skill (creative
director / UGC scriptwriter: 2 scripts sharing one message and angle, 3 hooks
each, shared creative direction, 8 shared b-roll clips). Section D is written
to match it. When `chopper` and this doc disagree on *format*, follow
`chopper`; when they disagree on *brand facts or copy rules*, this repo wins.

## The 3 focus products

Only these three — do not substitute other catalog items unless the user
explicitly asks:

| Product | Hard rules (never violate) |
|---|---|
| **Feather Knife** | $99.90. Rosewood handle. Blade pattern is **laser-applied** — never say hand-etched, hand-finished, or engraved. ~500-unit limited drops, ~3-month restock. Persona fit: **JOHN** (collector). |
| **BJORN Series Santoku** | Norse engravings on blade, dragon-sculpted **brass** bolster, hand-carved wooden handle. **Never reference Japanese origins or use the word "Japanese"** — santoku is a Japanese-origin knife shape but the brand never says so. Persona fit: **JOHN**. |
| **LOKI Blackout Edition** | $79.90. High-carbon steel, ebony handle, bottle opener built into the **handle** (not the blade/spine). Ships in a black branded box with magnetic closure. All-black remake of the #1-selling LOKI Viking Knife. Persona fit: **MIKE** (BBQ/grill self-buyer), **SARAH** (gift framing), general/deal-led for **VANCE**. |

Full detail: `brand-pack/01-brand/product-catalog.md`. Persona docs:
`brand-pack/02-personas/`.

**A creator saying a hard rule out loud is still a violation.** "Hand-etched"
in a talking-head line is worse than in a brief, because it ships in the
creator's own voice and can't be edited out in post.

## Universal copy rules (apply to every script, every product)

Same rulebook as `my-client` — these do not relax for UGC.

- **No spec-sheet jargon, ever**: no alloy codes, HRC/Rockwell numbers,
  "edge retention," "blade geometry," mm/gram specs. Say the plain material
  + the consequence ("hand-forged high-carbon steel… holds that edge").
  Full banned list and substitution table: process doc Section C.1.
- **The mechanic transfers, the words never do.** If a reference ad or an
  earlier script is the starting point, take its structure (hook type,
  pacing, beat order) — every sentence gets rewritten fresh. No verbatim
  source language, not even for an identical beat.
- **The offer resolves the subject, never replaces it.** Whatever the hook
  raises, the body must pay off *before* any offer appears. Offer lands
  ~60–80% through, never first/last, followed by 2–4 more beats. Only real
  offers exist: B2G2, B1G1, the % tiers — never invent one.
- **Never reuse the identical offer paragraph** across the scripts in one
  batch, or across product versions of the same concept.

## UGC-specific rules (on top of the above)

- **It has to be sayable.** Read every line out loud. If it needs a second
  breath, a comma the speaker won't hear, or a word nobody says at a grill,
  rewrite it. Contractions always.
- **The creator is a person, not a voiceover.** No "introducing," no
  "look no further," no stacked adjectives. One idea per sentence.
- **Never script a claim the creator can't personally stand behind.** No
  invented ownership duration, no fake gift recipient, no "I've had this for
  three years" unless the brief says the creator actually has.
- **Never script an on-screen caption that makes a claim the spoken line
  doesn't.** Captions reinforce; they don't add claims.
- **Every script must be shootable on an iPhone alone**, by one person, in
  the locations named in the brief. No gimbals, no second operator, no
  lighting kit. If a beat needs gear, cut the beat.

## Where things live

- `brand-pack/` — reference library (read-only source material).
  - `01-brand/` — product catalog + brand voice.
  - `02-personas/` — JOHN, MIKE, SARAH, VANCE.
  - `03-creator-direction/` — iPhone shoot direction + the b-roll library.
  - `04-approved-scripts/` — scripts that shipped and performed. Swipe the
    *mechanic*, never the lines.
  - `05-process/ugc-script-process.md` — **authoritative deliverable spec.**
- `ugc-scripts/` — output. One file per batch, named
  `YYYY-MM-DD-<product>-<persona>-<moment>.md`, from `_template.md`.
- `ugc-scripts/processed-concept-log.md` — dedup ledger. Every concept
  (persona × product × moment × angle) that ships gets logged. **Check this
  before writing** so the same angle isn't produced twice in a row.

## Delivery

Scripts are committed to `ugc-scripts/` in this repo. If the user also wants
them in Notion, mirror the `my-client` convention: one page per script in the
agreed database, matching the existing page structure/properties exactly —
and if the Notion connector isn't available in a given run, say so explicitly
rather than silently skipping delivery.

## Scaffold status

The product hard rules and copy rules above are authoritative. The brand-voice,
persona, and creator-direction docs are structured stubs — every field needing
content from the source brand pack is marked `TODO(brand-pack)`. **Do not
invent brand facts to fill them.** Fill from the source pack, or ask.
